WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Drop a metal rod between
two upright metal rails,

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.630
inside a magnetic field.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.570
At first it speeds up.

4
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.650
Then it gains speed more and more slowly,

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.620
settling towards a steady terminal speed.

6
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.210
Nothing touches it, yet
something holds it back.

7
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.620
So what decides how hard a
magnet brakes a moving conductor?

8
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.980
In this mission, you'll take
Faraday's law a step beyond,

9
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:29.550
with calculus, for a field and
an area that both change at once.

10
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.210
Then you'll steer a square loop
into a field and out again,

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.020
and find out when it feels a force at all.

12
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: find out what decides
how hard the magnet brakes the loop.
